#### SEC-008 — Prompt Injection & Insecure Output Handling in Incident Commander & Root Cause LLM
- Severity: Medium
- Confidence: Confirmed
- Location: `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/root-cause.ts:48-80`, `artifacts/context-app/src/App.tsx:301-308`
- Description: Incident chat messages (`serviceMessages`) and event descriptions (`serviceEvents`) are concatenated directly into the system prompt for the root-cause LLM without boundary delimitation or sanitization. An attacker ingesting alerts via webhooks can inject instructions into the LLM. Furthermore, the frontend generates executable `kubectl` commands using the service name returned by the LLM and provides a one-click clipboard copy feature for on-call engineers.
- Evidence:
```ts
// artifacts/api-server/src/routes/root-cause.ts:48-50
const msgCtx = recentMessages.slice(0, 10).map((m) =>
  `#${m.channel} @${m.author}: "${m.content}"`
).join("\n");
...
// artifacts/context-app/src/App.tsx:301-304
{ label: "Rollback deployment", cmd: `kubectl rollout undo deployment/${(rootCause.cascadePath[0] ?? "service").toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, "-")}` }
```
- Remediation: Enforce strict sanitization on ingested event strings, isolate untrusted user content in clearly demarcated user/context delimiters in LLM prompts, and whitelist allowed command patterns against pre-validated service identifiers.
- Effort: Medium

