### Performance

#### PRF-001 — High-Frequency 3-Second Dashboard Polling Triggers DB Write Mutations & LLM Load
- Severity: High
- Confidence: Confirmed
- Location: `artifacts/context-app/src/App.tsx:1850-1865`, `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/insights.ts:44-50, 433-436`, `routes/root-cause.ts:252`
- Description: The frontend dashboard automatically polls `/insights/summary` and `/insights/root-cause` every 3,000ms. On every request to `/insights/summary`, the server executes database `UPDATE` queries modifying service status. Furthermore, `/insights/root-cause` makes OpenAI API calls whenever the 30-second TTL cache expires. Multiple connected users will trigger lock contention on the database and rapid API token exhaustion.
- Evidence:
```ts
// artifacts/context-app/src/App.tsx
const ie = setInterval(gi, 3e3);
return () => clearInterval(ie);
```
- Remediation: Replace active 3-second polling with Server-Sent Events (SSE) or WebSockets, or increase polling interval to 20-30s. Remove all write mutations from `GET` endpoints.
- Effort: Medium

#### PRF-002 — Unbounded Memory Buffering in Document Upload Handler (OOM / DoS Risk)
- Severity: Medium
- Confidence: Confirmed
- Location: `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/upload.ts:18-29, 40`
- Description: Multer is configured with `memoryStorage()` allowing up to 20 files of 10MB each per upload batch. A single request can buffer up to 200MB into process heap memory. Multiple concurrent requests will cause Node.js heap exhaustion (OOM), crashing the API server.
- Evidence:
```ts
// artifacts/api-server/src/routes/upload.ts:18-29, 40
const storage = multer.memoryStorage();
const upload = multer({ storage, limits: { fileSize: 10 * 1024 * 1024 } });
router.post("/upload/docs", requireAuth, upload.array("files", 20), ...);
```
- Remediation: Stream file contents directly to object storage or disk using `multer.diskStorage`, and lower the max batch count and total payload size.
- Effort: Small

#### PRF-003 — Unbounded Conversation History Forwarded to OpenAI API
- Severity: Medium
- Confidence: Confirmed
- Location: `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/openai.ts:64, 74-82`
- Description: The chat endpoint retrieves all historical messages from the database and passes them all into OpenAI's completion API. As long-running conversations grow, request latency and billing costs scale linearly until context window limits are reached.
- Evidence:
```ts
// artifacts/api-server/src/routes/openai.ts:64
const history = await db.select().from(messages).where(eq(messages.conversationId, id));
...
messages: [
  { role: "system", content: systemPrompt },
  ...history.map((m) => ({ role: m.role, content: m.content })),
]
```
- Remediation: Implement a sliding context window (e.g. the last 10 messages) or summarize older messages before submitting to the model.
- Effort: Small

